      "writtenOn": "2019-03-14T14:53:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Coming in a bit late, but I thought of a possible improvement on this API design that lets you pass the query in a nicely typed, no-overhead style.\n\n/**\n * Base class for answer callbacks\n *\n * @param \u003cQ\u003e The type of the query\n * @param \u003cT\u003e The type of the parsed answer\n */\npublic abstract static class AnswerCallback\u003cQ, T\u003e {\n    /** @hide */\n    public final AnswerParser\u003cT\u003e parser;\n\n    public AnswerCallback(@NonNull AnswerParser\u003cT\u003e parser) {\n        this.parser \u003d parser;\n    };\n\n    public abstract void onAnswer(@NonNull Q query, @NonNull T answer);\n    public abstract void onParseException(@NonNull ParseException exception);\n    public abstract void onQueryException(@NonNull ErrnoException exception);\n}\n\n\nThen query become :\npublic void query(@Nullable Network, @NonNull byte[] query, @QueryFlag int flags,\n        @NonNull Handler handler, @NonNull AnswerCallback\u003c? super byte[], ? super byte[]\u003e);\n\nand\n\npublic void query(@Nullable Network, @NonNull String domain, @QueryClass int nsClass,\n        @QueryType int nsType, @QueryFlag int flags, @NonNull Handler handler,\n        @NonNull AnswerCallback\u003c? super String, ? super List\u003cInetAddress\u003e\u003e callback);",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "ff477e36475211c6797c54c122e77209688a4a6d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
