      "writtenOn": "2019-03-14T15:49:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Likewise I\u0027m tired. I should not try to think about bounds too hard past midnight, but now I won\u0027t be able to sleep if I don\u0027t try and write it right. Let\u0027s try it :\n\npublic abstract static class AnswerCallback\u003cQ, T, P extends T\u003e {\n  public final AnswerParser\u003cP\u003e parser;\n  public AnswerCallback(@NonNull AnswerParser\u003cP\u003e parser)\n  public abstract void onAnswer(@NonNull Q query, @NonNull T answer);\n  onparse\n  onquery\n}\n\npublic void query\u003cT\u003e(...byte[] query... ...AnwserCallback\u003c? super byte[], T, ? extends T\u003e)\npublic void query\u003cT\u003e(...String query... ...AnswerCallback\u003c? super String, T, ? extends T\u003e)\n\n\n...I think this is correct. It\u0027s also probably too complex for its own good, therefore I\u0027d favor the more obvious :\n\n\npublic abstract static class AnswerCallback\u003cQ, T\u003e {\n  public final AnswerParser\u003cT\u003e parser;\n  public AnswerCallback(@NonNull AnswerParser\u003cT\u003e parser)\n  public abstract void onAnswer(@NonNull Q query, @NonNull T answer);\n  onparse\n  onquery\n}\n\npublic void query\u003cT\u003e(...byte[] query... ...AnwserCallback\u003c? super byte[], T\u003e)\npublic void query\u003cT\u003e(...String query... ...AnswerCallback\u003c? super String, T\u003e)",
      "parentUuid": "855ad15d_9586a2c5",
